## Step 7: Install PEAR Dependencies

### Install HTTP_Client and dependencies:

    # Install via PEAR (will show deprecation warnings - this is normal)
    pear install HTTP_Client HTTP_Request Net_Socket Net_URL

    # Verify PEAR packages
    pear list

    # Test PHP can find HTTP_Client
    php -r 'require_once "HTTP/Client.php"; echo "HTTP_Client found\n";'

### If PEAR installation fails, install manually:

    # Download PEAR packages manually
    cd /tmp

    wget http://download.pear.php.net/package/HTTP_Client-1.2.1.tgz

    wget http://download.pear.php.net/package/HTTP_Request-1.4.4.tgz

    wget http://download.pear.php.net/package/Net_Socket-1.2.2.tgz

    wget http://download.pear.php.net/package/Net_URL-1.0.15.tgz

    # Extract and copy files
    for package in *.tgz; do tar -xzf "$package"; done

    mkdir -p /usr/share/pear/HTTP /usr/share/pear/Net

    cp HTTP_Client-*/Client.php /usr/share/pear/HTTP/

    cp HTTP_Request-*/Request.php /usr/share/pear/HTTP/

    cp Net_Socket-*/Socket.php /usr/share/pear/Net/

    cp Net_URL-*/URL.php /usr/share/pear/Net/

